WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:05.500
Federal Contract Information and Controlled Unclassified Information are central to CMMC

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.000
because the type of information in an environment helps determine the required protection

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.252
level and assessment scope.

00:00:10.252 --> 00:00:15.050
FCI is generally nonpublic information provided by or generated for the government under a

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:18.020
contract to develop or deliver a product or service.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:22.115
Publicly available information and simple transactional payment information are excluded

00:00:22.115 --> 00:00:23.056
from that concept.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:27.620
CUI is unclassified information that requires safeguarding or dissemination controls under

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.035
law,

00:00:28.035 --> 00:00:30.060
regulation, or government-wide policy.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.800
The CUI Registry and contract documentation help identify applicable categories and

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.215
handling expectations.

00:00:36.215 --> 00:00:39.520
CUI is not the same as classified national security information.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:40.945
Even though it is unclassified,

00:00:40.945 --> 00:00:45.300
its loss or unauthorized disclosure can still harm missions, individuals, programs,

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.240
business relationships, or national interests.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.965
Information identification must be deliberate.

00:00:49.965 --> 00:00:52.785
Teams need to understand what information the contract provides,

00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:56.705
what their work generates, which markings or clauses apply, where the information moves,

00:00:56.705 --> 00:00:58.920
and which systems or people interact with it.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.070
Data flow matters because protected information may appear in email,

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:06.310
collaboration platforms, engineering tools, ticketing systems, source repositories,

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:10.680
backups, exports, portable media, support records, and third-party services.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.935
Scope can often be improved by reducing unnecessary movement.

00:01:13.935 --> 00:01:18.440
Organizations may separate covered work, limit approved tools, clarify storage locations,

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:22.980
and avoid placing FCI or CUI in systems that were not designed or governed for it.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.580
When information status is unclear,

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.320
employees should follow organizational procedures and seek guidance from contract,

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.035
security, legal, or information-governance personnel.

00:01:31.035 --> 00:01:34.680
Guessing can create both protection gaps and unnecessary operational burden.
